INSERT INTO unlocks (thread, body) VALUES ('green-room', 'Why we''d rather give a $25 bar tab than $25 off. A tab costs the venue roughly a third of its face value in actual product — they hand over $25 of perceived value for well under ten dollars of cost. The host counts it as $25. Both sides come out ahead of a straight discount, and it''s the easiest concession a manager can say yes to without asking anyone.');
INSERT INTO unlocks (thread, body) VALUES ('green-room', 'Why we push for twelve dates instead of three. A new trivia night takes about six weeks to build a room — the first few are quiet no matter how good the show is. A three-date trial ends right as it starts working, and the venue concludes it didn''t. Twelve is the smallest booking that gives the night a fair test. That argument closes more bookings for us than the price does.');
INSERT INTO unlocks (thread, body) VALUES ('green-room', 'The $50 a night nobody quotes for. Game licensing, printing cards and answer sheets, batteries, replacement markers, the odd prize. It''s small enough to ignore and it''s the difference between a $225 night being worth doing and being break-even once you''ve driven there. Price your costs in before you name a number, because you won''t get to add them afterwards.');
INSERT INTO unlocks (thread, body) VALUES ('green-room', 'Why our one-off price is nearly double the recurring one, and why we don''t move on it. A single date carries all the setup, all the travel, all the prep, and none of it amortises across a run. Discounting a one-off to win it means the busiest, most awkward show you''ll do all month is also the worst paid. Quote it high and mean it.');
